- type: link
  label: createCommitOnBranch
  link: docs/graphql/mutations/createcommitonbranch
  routeSlug: docs/graphql/mutations/createcommitonbranch
  content:
    contentType: item
    itemVariant: mutation
    meta:
      name: createCommitOnBranch
      returnType: CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
      deprecated: false
      position:
        start:
          lineNumber: 17957
          column: 3
        end:
          lineNumber: 18006
          column: 6
    seo:
      title: createCommitOnBranch
      description: |-
        Appends a commit to the given branch as the authenticated user.

        This mutation creates a commit whose parent is the HEAD of the provided
        branch and also updates that branch to point to the new commit.
        It can be thought of as similar to `git commit`.

        ### Locating a Branch

        Commits are appended to a `branch` of type `Ref`.
        This must refer to a git branch (i.e.  the fully qualified path must
        begin with `refs/heads/`, although including this prefix is optional.

        Callers may specify the `branch` to commit to either by its global node
        ID or by passing both of `repositoryNameWithOwner` and `refName`.  For
        more details see the documentation for `CommittableBranch`.

        ### Describing Changes

        `fileChanges` are specified as a `FilesChanges` object describing
        `FileAdditions` and `FileDeletions`.

        Please see the documentation for `FileChanges` for more information on
        how to use this argument to describe any set of file changes.

        ### Authorship

        Similar to the web commit interface, this mutation does not support
        specifying the author or committer of the commit and will not add
        support for this in the future.

        A commit created by a successful execution of this mutation will be
        authored by the owner of the credential which authenticates the API
        request.  The committer will be identical to that of commits authored
        using the web interface.

        If you need full control over author and committer information, please
        use the Git Database REST API instead.

        ### Commit Signing

        Commits made using this mutation are automatically signed by GitHub if
        supported and will be marked as verified in the user interface.
    children:
      - nodeType: container
        children:
          - nodeType: header
            level: 2
            label: createCommitOnBranch
            showPageActions: true
            graphqlReturnType: CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
            graphqlArgs:
              - name: input
            graphqlDeprecated: false
            graphqlOperationType: mutation
          - nodeType: markdoc
            content:
              - Appends a commit to the given branch as the authenticated user.
              - >-
                This mutation creates a commit whose parent is the HEAD of the provided branch and also updates that
                branch to point to the new commit. It can be thought of as similar to .
              - Locating a Branch
              - >-
                Commits are appended to a  of type . This must refer to a git branch (i.e.  the fully qualified path
                must begin with , although including this prefix is optional.
              - >-
                Callers may specify the  to commit to either by its global node ID or by passing both of  and .  For
                more details see the documentation for .
              - Describing Changes
              - ' are specified as a  object describing and .'
              - >-
                Please see the documentation for  for more information on how to use this argument to describe any set
                of file changes.
              - Authorship
              - >-
                Similar to the web commit interface, this mutation does not support specifying the author or committer
                of the commit and will not add support for this in the future.
              - >-
                A commit created by a successful execution of this mutation will be authored by the owner of the
                credential which authenticates the API request.  The committer will be identical to that of commits
                authored using the web interface.
              - >-
                If you need full control over author and committer information, please use the Git Database REST API
                instead.
              - Commit Signing
              - >-
                Commits made using this mutation are automatically signed by GitHub if supported and will be marked as
                verified in the user interface.
          - nodeType: item-content
            variant: requires-scopes
            graphqlTypeName: createCommitOnBranch
            graphqlFieldName: createCommitOnBranch
            graphqlOperationType: mutation
          - nodeType: item-content
            variant: graphql-args
            label: Arguments
            labelTranslationKey: arguments.label
            graphqlTypeName: createCommitOnBranch
            graphqlFieldName: createCommitOnBranch
            graphqlOperationType: mutation
            graphqlSchema:
              - name: input
                type: CreateCommitOnBranchInput!
                description: Parameters for CreateCommitOnBranch
          - nodeType: item-content
            variant: return-type
            label: Return type
            labelTranslationKey: returnTypes.label
            schemaId: types/CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
            graphqlTypeName: CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
            graphqlOperationType: mutation
            graphqlFieldName: createCommitOnBranch
            graphqlSchema:
              type: CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
              description: Autogenerated return type of CreateCommitOnBranch
              fields:
                - name: clientMutationId
                  type: String
                  description: A unique identifier for the client performing the mutation.
                - name: commit
                  type: Commit
                  description: The new commit.
                - name: ref
                  type: Ref
                  description: The ref which has been updated to point to the new commit.
        panels:
          - children:
              - kind: graphql-query
                graphqlOperationData:
                  operationType: mutation
                  operationName: createCommitOnBranch
                  typeName: CreateCommitOnBranchPayload
